@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="privacy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: September 2026</p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">What we collect</h2>
    <p>
        When you register, we collect your full name and email address to
        create your account. When you submit a ticket, we store the ticket's
        title, description, category, priority, and any comments you add —
        this is the information needed to actually resolve your issue.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">How it's used</h2>
    <p>
        Your information is used only to operate the help desk: identifying
        who submitted or is assigned to a ticket, and displaying your name
        on comments and activity history so the right people can follow up.
        We don't use your data for marketing, and we don't sell or share it
        with third parties.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Who can see your tickets</h2>
    <p>
        End users can only see their own tickets. IT Agents and Admins can
        see all tickets, since resolving issues requires visibility across
        the team. This is enforced at the application level, not just hidden
        in the interface.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Data retention</h2>
    <p>
        Ticket history is retained so past issues can be referenced later —
        for example, to spot a recurring hardware problem. Accounts and
        their associated tickets can be removed on request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Contact</h2>
    <p>
        This is a portfolio/demo project built by Abulele Mndini. For any
        questions about this policy or the project itself, reach out via
        <a href="mailto:abulelemndini@gmail.com">abulelemndini@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
</div>